@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.778 = private unnamed_addr constant [26 x i8] c"builtin-variable-shadowing", align 1
@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.779 = private unnamed_addr constant [1081 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for variable (and function) assignments that use the same names\0Aas builtins.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AReusing a builtin name for the name of a variable increases the\0Adifficulty of reading and maintaining the code, and can cause\0Anon-obvious errors, as readers may mistake the variable for the\0Abuiltin and vice versa.\0A\0ABuiltins can be marked as exceptions to this rule via the\0A[`lint.flake8-builtins.ignorelist`] configuration option.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef find_max(list_of_lists):\0A    max = 0\0A    for flat_list in list_of_lists:\0A        for value in flat_list:\0A            max = max(max, value)  # TypeError: 'int' object is not callable\0A    return max\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef find_max(list_of_lists):\0A    result = 0\0A    for flat_list in list_of_lists:\0A        for value in flat_list:\0A            result = max(result, value)\0A    return result\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-builtins.ignorelist`\0A\0A## References\0A- [_Why is it a bad idea to name a variable `id` in Python?_](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/77552/id-is-a-bad-variable-name-in-python)\0A", align 1
