@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.872 = private unnamed_addr constant [358 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `if` branches with identical arm bodies.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIf multiple arms of an `if` statement have the same body, using `or`\0Abetter signals the intent of the statement.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aif x == 1:\0A    print(\22Hello\22)\0Aelif x == 2:\0A    print(\22Hello\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aif x == 1 or x == 2:\0A    print(\22Hello\22)\0A```\0A", align 1
