@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.944 = private unnamed_addr constant [736 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for docstrings that do not start with a capital letter.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe first non-whitespace character in a docstring should be\0Acapitalized for grammatical correctness and consistency.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef average(values: list[float]) -> float:\0A    \22\22\22return the mean of the given values.\22\22\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef average(values: list[float]) -> float:\0A    \22\22\22Return the mean of the given values.\22\22\22\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 257 \E2\80\93 Docstring Conventions](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/)\0A- [NumPy Style Guide](https://numpydoc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/format.html)\0A- [Google Python Style Guide - Docstrings](https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#38-comments-and-docstrings)\0A", align 1
