@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.975 = private unnamed_addr constant [573 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `os.getenv` calls with invalid default values.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIf an environment variable is set, `os.getenv` will return its value as\0Aa string. If the environment variable is _not_ set, `os.getenv` will\0Areturn `None`, or the default value if one is provided.\0A\0AIf the default value is not a string or `None`, then it will be\0Ainconsistent with the return type of `os.getenv`, which can lead to\0Aconfusing behavior.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport os\0A\0Aint(os.getenv(\22FOO\22, 1))\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport os\0A\0Aint(os.getenv(\22FOO\22, \221\22))\0A```\0A", align 1
